; claude: XPM, pictures as text (a palette and rows of characters),
; read and written by our own code: the sprites' file format (see
; Xpm.mli, and Sprite.of_xpm). Apart from graphics_images, which needs
; stb_image and curl, C code: pure OCaml, so the web backend can use it
; too. The first of the image formats we read and write ourselves
; rather than through stb_image. A private library (see
; graphics/core/dune), installed as part of elm_playground, whose
; Sprite uses it.
(library
 (name graphics_xpm)
 (package elm_playground)
 (wrapped false)
)
